# Motion Vocabulary

Every animated element must map to a named animation below. Never invent an
unnamed one-off effect, and never hardcode an easing, spring, duration, or
stagger value — import from `lib/motion-tokens.ts`.

```ts
import { motionTokens, revealTransition, magneticSpring } from "@/lib/motion-tokens";
// easeSignal [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1] | springMagnetic {150, 15, 0.8}
// springHover {300, 20} | durationReveal 0.8 | durationMicro 0.2 | staggerBase 0.06
// springAura {26, 20, 1.4} | auraMaxOffset 22px | durationDecode 3.5
// terminalCharMs 38 | terminalLineMs 90 | terminalColumnGapMs 260 (milliseconds)
```

| Name | Effect | Library |
|---|---|---|
| `SIGNAL_REVEAL` | `clip-path: inset()` unmask, left to right | Motion |
| `DECODE_TEXT` | Character scramble resolving left to right | Motion state |
| `CURSOR_TRACE` | Amber dot + spring-lagged trailing ring | Motion |
| `MAGNETIC_PULL` | ~10px shift toward cursor within 80px radius | Motion |
| `AURA_FOLLOW` | Blurred amber gradient layers drift toward the cursor's side | Motion + CSS |
| `WAVE_HOVER` | Sibling row ripple via per-index spring offset | Motion |
| `TERMINAL_PRINT` | Prompt types out, then lines print one at a time; columns run in sequence | Timers + CSS |
| `SCROLL_TRACE` | Line length bound to scroll progress, nodes light up | GSAP ScrollTrigger |
| `HORIZONTAL_PIN` | Pinned section, vertical scroll drives translateX | GSAP ScrollTrigger |
| `TILT_3D` | 3–6° `rotateX`/`rotateY` from cursor offset | Motion |
| `TAG_STAGGER` | Tags cascade in on card hover | Motion |
| `SCROLL_CUE` | Looping mono label pulse, dismissed via `useInView` | Motion |
| `WIPE_MASK` | Directional clip-path wipe for images | Motion |
| `PARALLAX_DRIFT` | Section-scoped `useScroll`/`useTransform` vertical drift | Motion |
| `COUNT_UP` | Numeric value animates 0 → target | Motion |
| `FADE_UP` | Opacity fade + 8px rise, optional per-index stagger | Motion |
| `ICON_LIFT` | Staggered entry, then 4px hover lift + tertiary→signal color | Motion |

Reusable implementations live in `components/motion/`. Prefer composing an
existing primitive over writing new animation code.

## Required gating

- Every animation needs a `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` fallback that resolves
  to an opacity fade or the static end state. Use `useReducedMotion()` from
  `motion/react`; `MotionConfig` alone does not cover `clip-path` or GSAP.
- `CURSOR_TRACE` and `HORIZONTAL_PIN` are fully disabled under reduced motion.
- `CURSOR_TRACE`, `MAGNETIC_PULL`, `TILT_3D`, `AURA_FOLLOW`, and interactive
  `TAG_STAGGER` are pointer-only: gate with `useFinePointer()` from
  `hooks/useFinePointer.ts` (`(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`).
- `TERMINAL_PRINT` is scroll-triggered, not pointer-gated: it runs on touch too.
  Under reduced motion it resolves to the finished output with no typing.
- `AURA_FOLLOW`'s cursor response is pointer-only, but the aura itself always
  renders. Touch and reduced motion show it at rest, not removed.
- Scroll-scrubbed GSAP timelines use `ease: "none"` and are created inside
  `gsap.matchMedia()` / `gsap.context()` so they clean up correctly.

## Design tokens

Colors, type scale, and layout tokens are CSS custom properties in
`app/globals.css`, surfaced as Tailwind utilities (`bg-void`, `text-primary`,
`text-signal`, `border-hairline`, `font-display`, `font-mono`, `text-display-xl`).
Full reference: `DESIGN.md`.
